---
description: Smart planning rules that keep RhinoDiet token use low
alwaysApply: true
---

Plan for token reduction before any exploration.

Compress the request. Cite memory ids. Assign the cheapest fitting worker. Do not paste graph bodies.

Prefer routing over repo tours. Do not full-repo scan when an ownership doc or Allowed paths already answer the question.

Single-domain work goes straight to that worker with a short handoff brief. Multi-domain work goes through the project manager. Assembly-style shared wiring runs last.

Every specialist handoff needs Agent, Allowed paths, Forbidden paths, Outcome, Inputs or constraints, and Out of scope. Name exact paths. Do not invent ownership.

Workers load only the brief and named Allowed files. They do not reload ownership docs when Allowed paths are complete. Interface reads outside Allowed paths are named exact paths only.

Completion reports stay short: changed paths, what shipped, blockers, test notes. No architecture re-reviews. No full-tree summaries.

Ask a short clarifying question before assuming missing paths. Prefer path-scoped handoffs over discovery.
